==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|super|continent}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|geology}} A very large [[continent]] that [[split]] into smaller ones in the [[earth|Earth]]’s [[geologic]] past.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Kent C. Condie|title=Mantle Plumes and Their Record in Earth History|publisher=Cambridge University Press|isbn=9780521014724|page=237|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=eMIXrEXORWkC&pg=PA237&dq=%22a+supercontinent%22&hl=&cd=1&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22a%20supercontinent%22&f=false|text=For a '''supercontinent''' to form requires a significant volume of continental crustal fragments that survive recycling into the mantle.}}
# A modern [[landmass]] composed of multiple continents, i.e. [[Afro-Eurasia]] or the [[Americas]].
#: {{cot|en|subcontinent}}

